cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use gpmeep, please cite this gpmeep software release and the upstream
  Meep paper listed in the references.
title: "gpmeep: CUDA-accelerated, multi-GPU Meep distribution"
type: software
version: 1.0.3
date-released: 2026-09-03
authors:
  - family-names: Yi
    given-names: Dong-Joon
    website: "https://iverydj.github.io/"
abstract: >-
  gpmeep extends the Meep finite-difference time-domain solver with a persistent
  FP32 CUDA execution layer, MPI-based multi-GPU operation, device-resident
  monitors and reductions, explicit backend control, and evidence-bound
  correctness and release validation.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Semiconductor-Nanophotonics-Laboratory/gpmeep-releases"
url: "https://iverydj.github.io/"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
keywords:
  - FDTD
  - GPU FDTD
  - CUDA FDTD
  - CUDA
  - GPU
  - Meep
references:
  - type: article
    title: "MEEP: A flexible free-software package for electromagnetic simulations by the FDTD method"
    authors:
      - family-names: Oskooi
        given-names: Ardavan F.
      - family-names: Roundy
        given-names: David
      - family-names: Ibanescu
        given-names: Mihai
      - family-names: Bermel
        given-names: Peter
      - family-names: Joannopoulos
        given-names: J. D.
      - family-names: Johnson
        given-names: Steven G.
    journal: Computer Physics Communications
    volume: 181
    issue: 3
    start: 687
    end: 702
    year: 2010
    doi: 10.1016/j.cpc.2009.11.008
